{:name "Migrating a savings cohort onto a different savings product"
 :tags #{:edn-only :cash-account-migrations :savings}
 ;; The case the whole design exists for: not evolving one product line
 ;; but splitting it. Two distinct savings products, and a cohort moved
 ;; from one to the other.
 ;;
 ;; This can only be exercised here. The API scenarios run on the micro
 ;; tier, which caps cash-account-products at one per product type, so
 ;; they can only reach the version-to-version case. The test-scenario
 ;; tier binds no such cap, which is what makes two savings products
 ;; possible at all.
 ;;
 ;; Nothing here moves an account. A preview decides about every account
 ;; in the cohort and writes a verdict per account — committing is the
 ;; scheduler's, and there is no API for it by design.
 :given [{:command :create-bank :args []}                          ; org-0,
                                                                   ; prod-0,
                                                                   ; acct-0
         {:command :create-product :args [:bank-0 :savings 100]}    ; prod-1
                                                                    ; super-saver
         {:command :publish-product :args [:prod-1]}
         {:command :create-product :args [:bank-0 :savings 365]}    ; prod-2
                                                                    ; mega-saver
         {:command :publish-product :args [:prod-2]}
         {:command :create-person-party :args [:bank-0]}            ; party-1
         {:command :open-account :args [:bank-0 :party-1 :prod-1]}  ; acct-1
         {:command :create-person-party :args [:bank-0]}            ; party-2
         {:command :open-account :args [:bank-0 :party-2 :prod-1]}] ; acct-2
 :when [{:command :create-migration :args [:bank-0 :prod-1 :prod-2]}
        {:command :preview-migration :args [:bank-0 :prod-1]}]
 ;; Both super-saver accounts are in the cohort and both would move: the
 ;; two products share a product type, which is the one compatibility
 ;; rule, and both accounts are open and hold a currency the target
 ;; allows.
 ;;
 ;; `accounts-moved` counts what a commit would move, not what this run
 ;; moved — a preview moves nothing, which is why the verdicts are
 ;; recorded as eligible rather than migrated. Accounts on prod-0 are
 ;; not in the cohort and get no verdict at all: being outside a
 ;; migration is not a reason for being left behind, and recording one
 ;; per account in the bank would bury the accounts that were considered.
 :then [{:command :assert-no-anomaly :args []}
        {:command :assert-migration-preview
         :args [{:dry-run true
                 :status :cash-account-migration-run-status-completed
                 :accounts-seen 2
                 :accounts-moved 2
                 :accounts-ineligible 0}]}
        {:command :assert-migration-verdicts
         :args [:bank-0 {:cash-account-migration-outcome-eligible 2}]}]}
